// bubbler profile: kitty
//
// A terminal emulator allocates its own pseudoterminals. bwrap's
// `--dev /dev` gives every sandbox a private devpts instance with its own
// index space (measured), so this needs no grant of its own and never a
// bind of the host's /dev/pts — which would hand over the host's ptys.
//
// The `tty` node is about how *bubbler's* stdio reaches your terminal and
// is unrelated to the ptys kitty makes for its own children; `tty "none"`
// is a reasonable setting for a GUI launch.
//
// Never share kitty's remote-control socket out of the sandbox. `kitten @`
// includes `launch`, so a reachable socket is command execution across
// the boundary, in whichever direction it was shared.
//
// A shell inside this sandbox sees only the private home. Share what you
// want to work on, e.g.
//     home-share "Projects" mode=rw
//
//
// `userns "disable"`: the shell inside cannot start bwrap, podman or a
// browser's inner sandbox; drop the line for a terminal that hosts those.
// Bare by design. Add:
//   dbus
//   portals
//     — kitty's org.freedesktop.portal.Settings read, without which it
//       cannot follow the desktop colour scheme (measured). It starts
//       either way. With `dbus` in place kitty also logs `Could not move
//       child process into a systemd scope` per child: that is its
//       StartTransientUnit call on org.freedesktop.systemd1, a name the
//       proxy does not carry. Harmless, and a `talk` for it would let the
//       sandbox start user units outside the sandbox.
//   notify
//     — desktop notifications, kitty's own and any a program inside sends
//       through it. Needs `dbus`.
//   network
//     — the only part of kitty that wants one is the update check, which
//       swallows the failure and reports version 0.0.0.
wayland
dri
userns "disable"
command "kitty"
